1141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (This project was completed independently as the final project for the Creator module. mai.premiumlinen is not my own business. I chose to work with an existing small brand and develop a complete content strategy based on its real context, limitations, and opportunities as a one-person business.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (This project required me to take responsibility for every stage of the process, from research and strategy to content creation, automation, testing, and documentation. Working alone meant every decision had to be made, tested, and refined without the support of a team. It was a valuable exercise in balancing creative thinking with practical problem-solving.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (If this brand were to grow into a larger operation, the first responsibility I would delegate would be content production, particularly carousel design and short-form video creation. These tasks are repetitive and time-intensive, making them well suited for collaboration or outsourcing. Strategy, positioning, and brand voice, however, are areas I would continue to oversee closely, as they provide the consistency that connects every piece of content.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 397 0 R
/E (Overall, this project showed me that for a small, one-person brand, success depends less on producing more content and more on building a system that is sustainable. Clear content pillars, thoughtful automation, and repeatable workflows make it possible to maintain quality without relying on constant manual effort.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
